course: dictionary
lesson: 15012
title: Bouncing back: resilience
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resilience is the ability to recover and keep going after something hard, sad or frightening. Think of it as bouncing back. «After losing the race, Sam felt sad, but he trained again the next day.» Sam showed resilience because he did not give up.
explain: Resilience is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say some resilience, not a resilience. «Ella needed resilience to finish the long swim.» You can also build resilience by learning from mistakes and asking for help when you need it.
explain: The word has two other meanings. A material with resilience springs back into shape: «The rubber ball bounced back after it was squashed.» A place or system can have resilience too: «The town built stronger drains, so it could cope with heavy rain.»
fact: Resilience is a noun, and it is uncountable: say some resilience, not a resilience.
fact: «Resilience» means the ability to recover and keep going after something hard, sad or frightening.
fact: «Resilience» can also mean a material springing back into shape after being bent, squashed or stretched.
fact: Useful phrases are build resilience, show resilience and emotional resilience.
fact: You can build resilience by learning from mistakes and asking for help when things go wrong.
exercise: «Even after losing the race, Sam kept training and showed great resilience.» What does resilience mean here? | Feeling no emotions at all | Winning every race without trying | *Bouncing back and carrying on after a setback | Running very fast
exercise: In science, a rubber band stretches and then springs back into shape. This shows which kind of resilience? | *The ability of a material to spring back | Emotional resilience | The ability of a town to cope with floods | Giving up when things go wrong
exercise: Which phrase means learning to bounce back from hard times? | Lose hope | Ignore the problem | *Build resilience | Hide away
test: «The town built higher walls and better drains, so it could cope with heavy rain.» What quality does the town show? | Laziness | Sadness | Silence | *Resilience
test: «Olivia wanted to give up, but she asked her teacher for help and tried again.» Which word best describes Olivia? | Bored | Careless | *Resilient | Shy
exam: Which sentence uses resilience correctly? | She showed a resilience after the fall. | *She showed some resilience after the fall. | She showed resilient after the fall. | She showed resiliences after the fall.
